  "image": "assets/locations/discord/f05baf1527b792a1f7788f411a3113824db47a00c747d4adee4700f2cf124efa.webp",
  "imageAlt": "The preserved coastal setting of Crustacean Cove",
  "imageCaption": "Crustacean Cove — previously reviewed coastal location artwork.",
  "body": "<p>Crustacean Cove is a sheltered stretch of Gael’s coast, about two miles from the <a href=\"#tower-of-gael\">Tower</a> in the recorded approach. The shore provides food and materials; the underwater cave beneath it leads into a much more dangerous descent. The place is named during a harvesting expedition, before the later shipwreck and refugee proposals.</p><h2 id=\"cove-naming-expedition\">Choosing the coast, and giving it a name</h2><p>Scribonia would rather return to the Cathedral, but Saray wants to gather coastal materials for Gartina’s project. Dale supports the coast. Saray leads them along hidden cliff paths through the rain, and Scribonia recognizes promising rock and tide conditions from his reading.</p><p>Gathering proves less comfortable than finding the spot. Saray locates oysters but comes up chilled; Dale spots large crabs he cannot readily reach. Gartina finds eggs among fossilized coral and returns shivering. While the group is still working out how to harvest the water below, Gartina proposes the name Crustacean Cove, and Scribonia agrees.</p><p>They warm themselves, change their approach and gather oysters, a large crab and eggs identified as belonging to a cold-water coral drake. The day’s original purpose is achieved before they risk the deeper cave. Scribonia accepts an eel form despite his dislike of the water; Gartina explores as a cold-tolerant shark. Dale later runs back to the Tower for breathing bubbles so he and Saray can join them.</p><h2 id=\"cove-underwater-descent\">Four swords over a dark descent</h2><p>Lights mark the cave entrance far below the shore. Scribonia scouts ahead, senses danger and turns back rather than continue without the others. Once the company is together, the swim leads through darkness to a hollow lit by four giant swords. A deep pit opens beneath them.</p><p>Two enormous eel guardians rise from below. Lightning tears through the water, and Dale is knocked out and begins to sink. The fight continues rather than becoming an easy exploration of the temple. Gartina’s changing sea-creature form keeps her in the struggle; Dale rallies and warns her in time to help prevent another fatal blow.</p><p>The company defeats those opponents, but more guardians are already coming up from the depths. Gartina carries Scribonia as they withdraw. They reach the surface with the rain still falling and their harvest still on shore. She attempts to heal him; the closing scene does not supply a complete recovery account. Dale offers the exhausted Saray a ride back toward the Tower.</p><p>The location’s opening description identifies an underwater cave and a temple beneath the cove. This visit establishes the approach, four-sword hollow, guardians and retreat. It does not establish a cleared temple, its full floor plan or the origin of every structure below. The shore’s usefulness cannot be extended into a promise of safety in the deep.</p><h2 id=\"cove-wreck\">A wreck as a possible resource</h2><p><a href=\"#dale\">Dale</a> proposes salvaging timber for a longhouse if the ship is beyond repair. <a href=\"#gartina\">Gartina</a> supports considering the idea but does not know what the tide has done to the remains. A proposal to reuse the vessel is not evidence that it was inspected, declared irreparable or successfully dismantled.</p><p>The plan connects coastal wreckage to the <a href=\"#gael-refugee-settlement\">refugee community near the Tower</a>. Material might become shelter, but the people affected have yet to be consulted at this point in the conversation. Neither Dale nor Gartina acquires authority over them by proposing help.</p><h2 id=\"cove-ordinary-company\">Returning to the coast between expeditions</h2>\n<p>Saelihn walks the coast after Coralyn brings her back to Gael. At the Cove she meets Severina and Kar’nak, delivers sending stones and discusses material shortages. Her report that Eovar’s magical trade may close remains a rumor. Severina promises to protect her during an approaching molt; the transformation itself is not shown.</p><p>Fenwick later sits by the water with an illusory map, talks with Kar’nak about the island’s incomplete exploration and collects shells for hoped-for fertilizer. Their discussion of roads and a town adds future work to the Cove’s history, without changing the map or establishing a finished settlement.</p>\n<h2 id=\"cove-separate-geography\">A cove with more than one history</h2><p>The cove’s named harvesting trip and guarded descent belong here. The earlier wheel encounter is explicitly placed in the Cathedral in Gael’s ruined city. The coastal company later chooses this outing instead of returning there. Shared adventurers and a shared island do not make every ruin one site.</p><p>The refugee ship’s route and detailed crash remain incompletely recovered. The ship near the Cove and the people sheltering around the Tower remain different locations within the same community history. No completed longhouse, final salvage operation, permanent refugee government or fully surveyed underwater plan is established.</p><p class=\"place-context-links\"><strong>Connected histories</strong> <a href=\"#gael\">Gael</a></p>",
